    "detailed_description": "Atompunk cooking simulator with a twist.<br><br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2886610/extras/55ed92365449d5b3b36fb1ff9f627b3b.poster.avif?t=1716416527\" width=600 height=338 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2886610/extras/55ed92365449d5b3b36fb1ff9f627b3b.webm?t=1716416527\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2886610/extras/55ed92365449d5b3b36fb1ff9f627b3b.mp4?t=1716416527\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >MANAGE YOUR COZY SPACESHIP DINER</h2><br>Manage a small 1950s-reminiscent diner that orbits the planet in open space. Based on the planet's rotations, the inside environment changes, creating three different playing conditions. Learn to manage the resources carefully and lead the diner to success!<br><br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2886610/extras/d0c5e95c91e4f84c330282640f2d8802.poster.avif?t=1716416527\" width=600 height=338 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2886610/extras/d0c5e95c91e4f84c330282640f2d8802.webm?t=1716416527\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2886610/extras/d0c5e95c91e4f84c330282640f2d8802.mp4?t=1716416527\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >FUN GAMEPLAY - SERIOUS MESSAGE</h2><br>Doppel Diner is not just a story about a diner influenced by external weather conditions. It is also a metaphor for managing the emotional states of bipolar disorder: a mental illness that causes dramatic mood shifts. The game's goal is not to explain what bipolar disorder is, but to offer an experience of <i>how it might feel like</i> to spark important conversations and shift the stigma around mental health.",
    "about_the_game": "Atompunk cooking simulator with a twist.<br><br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2886610/extras/55ed92365449d5b3b36fb1ff9f627b3b.poster.avif?t=1716416527\" width=600 height=338 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2886610/extras/55ed92365449d5b3b36fb1ff9f627b3b.webm?t=1716416527\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2886610/extras/55ed92365449d5b3b36fb1ff9f627b3b.mp4?t=1716416527\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >MANAGE YOUR COZY SPACESHIP DINER</h2><br>Manage a small 1950s-reminiscent diner that orbits the planet in open space. Based on the planet's rotations, the inside environment changes, creating three different playing conditions. Learn to manage the resources carefully and lead the diner to success!<br><br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2886610/extras/d0c5e95c91e4f84c330282640f2d8802.poster.avif?t=1716416527\" width=600 height=338 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2886610/extras/d0c5e95c91e4f84c330282640f2d8802.webm?t=1716416527\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2886610/extras/d0c5e95c91e4f84c330282640f2d8802.mp4?t=1716416527\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >FUN GAMEPLAY - SERIOUS MESSAGE</h2><br>Doppel Diner is not just a story about a diner influenced by external weather conditions. It is also a metaphor for managing the emotional states of bipolar disorder: a mental illness that causes dramatic mood shifts. The game's goal is not to explain what bipolar disorder is, but to offer an experience of <i>how it might feel like</i> to spark important conversations and shift the stigma around mental health.",
